# Local development — leave this EMPTY.
#
# Empty means every request is relative (/api, /uploads, /socket.io), which the
# Vite dev server proxies. Where it proxies *to* is set in vite.config.js:
#
#   npm run dev        → local Flask on :5000
#   npm run dev:prod   → the live API at api.f2hmarket.com:8443
#
# Do not put an absolute URL here. Pointing the browser straight at the API
# bypasses the proxy and breaks dev twice over: the API rejects the localhost
# origin (CORS), and the SameSite auth cookie is not sent cross-site, so
# nothing is ever authenticated. Both fail at the network layer with nothing
# useful in the UI, which reads as "the whole site is broken".
VITE_API_URL=
